            "review_text": "Tom H\nLondon, United Kingdom8 contributions\n0\nMenu design issue\nMay 2020\nI ordered cheesy burrito-sauteed ground beef but there is no beef inside the burrito. I called the restaurant and they said there was no beef because i left a note in my order said “no optional protein”. The menu design is certainly confusing for non-vegan or non-vegetarian! Protein can be beans, potato, etc, can be anything that has protein. I left a note “no optional protein” because I was wary of this being protein powder or additional beef. It was certainly a letdown when I got the unexpectedly healthy dinner. I hope the menu can be communicated more clearly in the future. The food in itself is quite average. A typical Tex-Mex burrito with average filling and quite underwhelming wrap.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 29, 2020",
